  "notes": [
    "Regular -AR verb — follows standard -AR endings with no exceptions",
    "Past participle: *enamorado* (regular; also a very common adjective meaning \"in love\")",
    "Means \"to win someone's heart\" or \"to make (someone) fall in love\" — *la enamoró con su sonrisa* (he won her heart with his smile)",
    "Reflexive *enamorarse (de)* is far more common in everyday speech and means \"to fall in love (with)\": *me enamoré de ella al instante* (I fell in love with her instantly)",
    "Related: *amor* (love), *enamorado/a* (in love; also \"sweetheart\" as a noun), *enamoramiento* (infatuation, the state of falling in love)"
  ],
